# Developed in tandem with samples/GCP/ProcessEngineering's own
# Project_Plan_Export_Agent and Project_Plan_Reviewer_Agent.
# Exports the current Enterprise Agile Portfolio Backlog or Proposal Response as an
# illustrative Microsoft Project / ProjectLibre interchange-format (MSPDI XML) project plan,
# audited and refined in an iterative review loop against schedule compliance, concurrency,
# holiday calendars, resource allocations, and project GOAL alignment.
{
    include "config/llm_config.hocon",

    "metadata": {
        "description": "Exports the current Enterprise Agile Portfolio Backlog or Proposal Response as a Microsoft Project / ProjectLibre (MSPDI XML) project plan, audited and refined in an iterative review loop for schedule compliance, concurrency, resourcing, and goal alignment.",
        "tags": ["portfolio", "proposal", "project-plan", "process-engineering-port"],
        "sample_queries": [
            "Export the portfolio backlog as a project plan.",
            "Give me an MS Project file for our proposal response."
        ]
    },

    "tools": [
        {
            "name": "Project_Plan_Export_Agent_Main",

            "function": {
                "description": """
I export the current Enterprise Agile Portfolio Backlog or Proposal Response as a real Microsoft
Project / ProjectLibre interchange-format (MSPDI XML) project plan, audited and refined in an iterative
review loop to ensure strict timescale compliance, concurrency, holiday handling, and resource allocation
matching the engagement goals. I always generate a PERT/CPM network diagram alongside it.
""",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "inquiry": {"type": "string", "description": "The user's project-plan-export request."}
                    },
                    "required": ["inquiry"]
                }
            },

            "instructions": """
# ROLE
You orchestrate the Project Plan Export and Schedule Audit Loop:
1. Project_Plan_Export_Agent determines planning parameters and exports the MSPDI XML project plan and PERT/CPM diagram.
2. Project_Plan_Reviewer_Agent audits the exported project plan for timescale compliance, concurrency, holiday handling, resource allocations, and goal satisfaction, writing feedback to its mailbox and approval status.
3. You decide whether to repeat the review cycle using loop_control.
4. Project_Plan_Export_Agent applies feedback on any REVISION pass before re-exporting.
You never author the XML or calculate schedule timings yourself.

# REQUIRED SEQUENCE
1. Call reset_loop_state once (no commentary) -- clears stale approval/iteration state from an
   earlier request and claims the turn lock. If it returns "status": "ERROR", STOP immediately and
   report that error message verbatim.
2. Call Project_Plan_Export_Agent, passing the user's request text verbatim as "inquiry". If it asks
   a clarifying question (e.g. genuinely ambiguous artifact type) or returns an ERROR, call
   release_pipeline_lock_for_turn FIRST, THEN STOP immediately and report that reply verbatim.
3. Call Project_Plan_Reviewer_Agent, passing the user's request text verbatim as "inquiry" (it inspects
   the exported project plan and source backlog to perform the quality audit).
4. Call loop_control with required={"project_plan_review_status": "APPROVED"} and max_iterations=2.
   - If "verdict" is "CONTINUE": call Project_Plan_Export_Agent again, passing "inquiry" verbatim -- it will
     pick up the reviewer's feedback itself via load_iteration_feedback, apply the required adjustments,
     and re-export the plan. Then go back to step 3.
   - If "verdict" is "STOP": call release_pipeline_lock_for_turn FIRST, then proceed to step 5.
5. Call format_review_status_summary (no arguments) to retrieve the final audit verdict.
6. Report in plain language that the project plan was exported, stating the exact XML file path,
   the companion PERT/CPM chart path, start/finish dates, timescale compliance, resource allocations,
   and the review audit outcome. The tool's own result also mentions a PERT/CPM network diagram generated alongside it -- relay that path too, in the same reply.
   If the export result contains a WARNING (the plan overran a stated target_duration_weeks), relay that warning's own text verbatim.
""",
            "tools": [
                "reset_loop_state",
                "release_pipeline_lock_for_turn",
                "Project_Plan_Export_Agent",
                "Project_Plan_Reviewer_Agent",
                "loop_control",
                "format_review_status_summary",
                "load_iteration_feedback"
            ],
            "middleware": ${pipeline_middleware}
        },

        {
            "name": "Project_Plan_Export_Agent",

            "function": {
                "description": "Determines export parameters and exports the saved portfolio backlog or proposal response as an MSPDI XML project plan and PERT chart, adjusting on revision passes.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "inquiry": {"type": "string", "description": "The user's project-plan-export request."}
                    },
                    "required": ["inquiry"]
                }
            },

            "instructions": """
# ROLE
You export the current Enterprise Agile Portfolio Backlog or Proposal Response as an illustrative
Microsoft Project / ProjectLibre (MSPDI XML) project plan, from whatever is already saved on disk.

# REVISION MODE (REVIEW FEEDBACK)
First, call load_iteration_feedback with channel="project_plan_reviewer".
If it returns feedback containing issues:
- Review the instructions and recommendations from the schedule auditor.
- Adjust parameters (e.g. enforce target_duration_weeks, ensure holiday_calendar="uk", adjust resource allocations).
- Re-call export_project_plan with the adjusted parameters.
- Report what adjustments were made.

# DETERMINE schema_type FIRST (NEW GENERATION)
If not in revision mode:
Check whether "inquiry" itself names a domain:
- If it explicitly says "backlog" / "portfolio backlog" / "epics" / "WSJF", schema_type = "portfolio_backlog".
- If it explicitly says "proposal" / "proposal response" / "RtP" / "response", schema_type = "proposal_response".
- Otherwise, ask the user to clarify whether they mean the portfolio backlog or the proposal response.

# OPTIONAL PLANNING ASSUMPTIONS (extract from the user's own wording -- never fabricate any of these when not stated)
- resources: if the user names roles/people with a % allocation (e.g. "Programme Delivery Manager (50%)",
  "Lead Business Analyst (100%)", "Solution Architect (50%)"), pass resources=[{"name": "<role>", "allocation_percent": <number>}, ...].
  Only include entries the user actually named -- never invent a role or guess a percentage that wasn't stated.
  If no allocation is named at all, omit resources entirely rather than guessing 100% for everyone.
- target_duration_weeks: if the user states a target length (e.g. "12-week", "running over 3 months"), convert to weeks and pass it.
- holiday_calendar: if the user says to honor UK/British public or bank holidays, pass holiday_calendar="uk". Only "uk" is supported.
- start_date: if the user specifies a start date, pass ISO "YYYY-MM-DD".

# EXECUTION
Call export_project_plan with the determined parameters.
Report the export outcome, file paths, and any warnings.
""",
            "tools": ["export_project_plan"]
        },

        {
            "name": "Project_Plan_Reviewer_Agent",

            "function": {
                "description": "Audits the quality, schedule compliance, concurrency, calendar/holidays, resourcing, and goal satisfaction of the exported project plan.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "inquiry": {"type": "string", "description": "The user's request, passed through for context."}
                    },
                    "required": ["inquiry"]
                }
            },

            "instructions": """
# ROLE
You are a Principal Project Controls and Schedule Auditor performing a QUALITY AUDIT on the
exported Microsoft Project (MSPDI XML) project plan and companion PERT/CPM chart.

# CRITICAL OPERATIONAL RULES
1. Call inspect_project_plan. Reload it every turn.
2. Call load_portfolio_backlog or load_requirements_summary to inspect the source grounding and project goals.
3. Universal project-agnostic audit principles: never hardcode fixed assumptions from any sample prompt.
   Evaluate dynamically against the user's requested timescale, resources, holiday calendar, and deliverables.

# AUDIT CRITERIA
1. STRICT TIMESCALE COMPLIANCE & ZERO OVERRUN:
   - If the engagement specifies a target timescale (e.g. 12 weeks), verify that the finish date does NOT
     exceed the target duration. Any unmanaged calendar overrun is an automatic failure.
2. CONCURRENCY & PARALLEL WORKSTREAMS:
   - Verify that independent phases or tasks run concurrently where appropriate, rather than a purely linear waterfall cascade.
3. CALENDAR & HOLIDAY INTEGRITY:
   - Verify non-working days (weekends) and holiday exceptions (e.g. UK bank holidays if requested).
4. RESOURCE ALLOCATION & ASSIGNMENTS:
   - Verify that named roles and allocation percentages match the engagement specification.
   - Verify that resources are properly mapped to tasks with correct units.
5. DELIVERABLES & GOAL SATISFACTION:
   - Verify that all requested phases and deliverables are present as tangible milestones or tasks.

# AUDIT OUTCOME & FEEDBACK CONTRACT
1. IF ANY CRITERIA FAIL:
   - Compile a structured list of specific defects and actionable instructions:
     `[{"issue": "<detailed issue description>", "instruction": "<exact instruction on how to adjust schedule/resourcing>"}]`
   - CALL save_iteration_feedback with:
     `feedback_data={"status": "REVISION REQUIRED", "data": issues_list}`
     `channel="project_plan_reviewer"`
   - Output a clear summary of findings explaining why revision is required.
2. IF ALL CRITERIA PASS:
   - CALL save_iteration_feedback with:
     `feedback_data={"status": "PROJECT_PLAN_REVIEW_APPROVED", "data": []}`
     `channel="project_plan_reviewer"`
   - Output: "PROJECT_PLAN_REVIEW_APPROVED: Project plan satisfies all timescale constraints, concurrency, resource allocations, and core goals."
""",
            "tools": [
                "inspect_project_plan",
                "load_portfolio_backlog",
                "load_requirements_summary",
                "save_iteration_feedback"
            ]
        },

        {
            "name": "reset_loop_state",
            "function": {"description": "Clears stale approval/iteration-counter state from an earlier request and claims pipeline lock. Takes no meaningful arguments."},
            "class": "reset_loop_state_tool.ResetLoopStateCodedTool"
        },
        {
            "name": "release_pipeline_lock_for_turn",
            "function": {"description": "Safely releases THIS turn's own pipeline lock. Takes no meaningful arguments."},
            "class": "release_pipeline_lock_tool.ReleasePipelineLockForTurnCodedTool"
        },
        {
            "name": "loop_control",
            "function": {
                "description": "Decides whether the generate/review loop should continue or stop.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "required": {"type": "object", "description": "Approval-state keys/values that must all be present to stop as approved."},
                        "max_iterations": {"type": "integer"}
                    },
                    "required": ["required", "max_iterations"]
                }
            },
            "class": "loop_control_tool.LoopControlCodedTool"
        },
        {
            "name": "load_iteration_feedback",
            "function": {
                "description": "Reads and drains a feedback mailbox channel.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "channel": {"type": "string", "description": "Which mailbox channel to read, e.g. \"project_plan_reviewer\"."}
                    },
                    "required": ["channel"]
                }
            },
            "class": "load_iteration_feedback_tool.LoadIterationFeedbackCodedTool"
        },
        {
            "name": "save_iteration_feedback",
            "function": {
                "description": "Writes feedback and approval status to an iteration feedback channel.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "feedback_data": {"type": "object", "description": "Object with status and data list."},
                        "channel": {"type": "string", "description": "Channel name, e.g. \"project_plan_reviewer\"."}
                    },
                    "required": ["feedback_data", "channel"]
                }
            },
            "class": "save_iteration_feedback_tool.SaveIterationFeedbackCodedTool"
        },
        {
            "name": "format_review_status_summary",
            "function": {"description": "Renders the current review status summary for project plan review."},
            "class": "format_review_status_tool.FormatReviewStatusCodedTool"
        },
        {
            "name": "export_project_plan",
            "function": {
                "description": "Exports the current saved Enterprise Agile Portfolio Backlog or Proposal Response as an MSPDI project plan file, plus a companion PERT/CPM network diagram generated from the same scheduled tasks.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "schema_type": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "enum": ["portfolio_backlog", "proposal_response"],
                            "description": "Which saved artifact to export a project plan from."
                        },
                        "start_date": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Optional ISO \"YYYY-MM-DD\" project start date. Defaults to today if omitted."
                        },
                        "resources": {
                            "type": "array",
                            "description": "Optional list of named resources with their % allocation, extracted from the user's own wording -- never fabricated.",
                            "items": {
                                "type": "object",
                                "properties": {
                                    "name": {"type": "string", "description": "The role or person's name, as the user stated it."},
                                    "allocation_percent": {"type": "number", "description": "0-100, as the user stated it."}
                                },
                                "required": ["name", "allocation_percent"]
                            }
                        },
                        "target_duration_weeks": {
                            "type": "number",
                            "description": "Optional target project length in weeks, if the user stated one (approximate months as 4 weeks each). A post-hoc overrun check only -- never compresses the schedule to fit."
                        },
                        "holiday_calendar": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "enum": ["uk"],
                            "description": "Only \"uk\" is supported. Set when the user asks to honor UK/British public or bank holidays."
                        }
                    },
                    "required": ["schema_type"]
                }
            },
            "class": "project_plan_export_tool.ExportProjectPlanCodedTool"
        },
        {
            "name": "inspect_project_plan",
            "function": {
                "description": "Parses and returns structured quality and schedule metrics for the exported project plan (MSPDI XML).",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "schema_type": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "enum": ["portfolio_backlog", "proposal_response"],
                            "description": "Which project plan to inspect. Defaults to portfolio_backlog."
                        }
                    }
                }
            },
            "class": "inspect_project_plan_tool.InspectProjectPlanCodedTool"
        },
        {
            "name": "load_portfolio_backlog",
            "function": {"description": "Loads the existing Enterprise Agile Portfolio Backlog JSON, if any. Takes no meaningful arguments."},
            "class": "load_portfolio_backlog_tool.LoadPortfolioBacklogCodedTool"
        },
        {
            "name": "load_requirements_summary",
            "function": {"description": "Loads the saved requirements summary, if any. Takes no meaningful arguments."},
            "class": "load_requirements_summary_tool.LoadRequirementsSummaryCodedTool"
        }
    ]
}
